STATUS 2026-08-11: scope breakdown documented. Not started; out of session
scope. Sub-tickets 31a-31d PROPOSED, not auto-created — maintainer splits
when ready.

Scope: Self-hosted inference engines expose runtime knobs that influence
throughput / latency without affecting model identity:
  - prefix caching (KV cache reuse across requests) — vLLM, SGLang
  - speculative decoding (draft model parallel verification) — vLLM,
    SGLang, possibly LlamaCpp
  - continuous batching (in-flight batching) — mostly internal, surfaced
    as a counter, not a knob
OpenAI/Anthropic don't expose these. Cloud alternatives are model-side
fixed.

Proposed sub-tickets:
  31a — research: which knobs are runtime-tunable vs require restart
        per engine (vLLM, SGLang, LlamaCpp). Source: each engine's docs.
  31b — value object: Langertha::Runtime::Knobs with engine-gated
        sub-objects (VLLM::Knobs, SGLang::Knobs, LlamaCpp::Knobs) —
        each engine declares what it accepts
  31c — wire: per-engine request body or extra_body extension. vLLM
        accepts extra_body fields for speculative decoding and prefix
        cache hints; SGLang similar
  31d — role: Langertha::Role::RuntimeKnobs on the relevant engines
        with capabilities gating (prefix_caching, speculative_decoding
        boolean checks)
  31e — tests: engine_capabilities test per knob; offline request-body
        extension test; live gated on running engine

Out of scope (separate tickets):
  - Continuous-batching visibility (it's an internal scheduler flag,
    not a user knob)
  - Multi-LoRA hot-swap (vLLM-specific, different concern)
